Z||000000||I wish I had a GT||06-25-2001||07:38 PM||||I'm pretty sure pontiac never made fiero convertables, am I correct?  Does anyone have an estimate of what it would cost to make one, or have one made?<P>------------------<BR>Larry H||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-25-2001||08:09 PM||||Pontiac never made a convertible Fiero.  But there were some dealers who did an upgrade of a Fiero into a convertible.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Convert_1.jpg"> <P>I think this blue one at the OOB show was one such car..  There are some talented people out there who have made some real nice convertibles.  The two big challenges are to find an attractive convertible top kit. The second is to reinforce the bottom of the car.  The loss of the roof makes the car bend in the middle.<BR>I have seen some real hack jobs that pass off for convertibles.  The top kits when avaialable were selling for $2.5K several years ago and there are very few around today if any.<BR>There are some vendors (check vendor list) who will take on the challenge, but you would need to call them for a cost estimate. Bob Stieger had this one on his lot last month.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/convertiblered.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tweek||06-25-2001||08:49 PM||||This Indy was also AT the show, but not IN the show. (thats why hes in the parkin lot next to me lol)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/shows/oob/oob6-16-01_0028.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||06-25-2001||10:02 PM|||| Chris Moore has what I think is the nicest convertible top on one of his GTs.. It was made by Automoda, and they don't make them anymore... cost about $6,000 in 1991.. I have a ton of pics of it on my website, but here is one:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/daytonatrack.jpg">  <P>V8 Archie recently bought an Automoda top from ebay and I guess he is trying to make a replica of it to sell? Haven't heard anymore on that, but I can't imagine its going to be cheap.<P>And here are 2 other convertibles I've seen at shows:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/show13.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/mycar4.jpg"> <BR>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">    <P>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 06-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
