Z||000010||northstar87||06-26-2001||09:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>I always wondered, how are the seatbelts modified in these droptops?  And (like I give a damn) how are these mods to the belts legal?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi,<BR>   Come to the Michigan show, Carlisle, Virginia or the Chicago show and see mine.  It is very nice and strong.  Well thought out.  I even have the Northstar in the back.  The frame was way over done.  I did not think I would have a problem.  It works perfect.<P>Chris Moore||||reg||1
Z||000011||qwikgta||06-26-2001||09:37 PM||||Northstar87 (chris) what do you mean that the frame was overdone.  I am looking at cutting the top off my 87 coupe but before I start I have been trying to get info on the frame reenforcement.  Do you have any additional advice, or any at this point. Pics of the underside would be great, so far no one has been able to produce pics or diagrams for me to copy.<P>Thanks in advance<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000012||northstar87||06-26-2001||09:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by qwikgta:<BR><B>Northstar87 (chris) what do you mean that the frame was overdone.  I am looking at cutting the top off my 87 coupe but before I start I have been trying to get info on the frame reenforcement.  Do you have any additional advice, or any at this point. Pics of the underside would be great, so far no one has been able to produce pics or diagrams for me to copy.<P>Thanks in advance<P>Rob<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi Rob,<BR>  Come to one of the shows that I listed and you can spend all day taking pictures and whatever else you needed.  I wish I could help you out more.  Just ask and I will do my best.  It is a square, x, and rides along the curves of the space frame.  Really nice.   <P><BR>Chris Moore<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||qwikgta||06-29-2001||08:01 PM||||Chris...see ya in VA<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
